2. Which verification I ran: I ran the focused fact-sim MCP correctness suite with `engine_test` using `action="run"`, `engines=["event-fast-worker","event-fast-par"]`, `reruns=0`, `strictFinalParity=false`, `stopOnFirstFailure=true`. Result: `PASS`, 27/27 cases passed, 0 warnings, 0 failures.

3. Residual risk: the standard suite still passes, but it does not explicitly prove the hidden failing case was a `stopGroups`-backed live graph. The remaining risk is limited to some other live-graph serialization edge outside this path; I did not see any regression in the covered fast-engine scenarios.
